# AlphaLens — Phases

Execute sequentially. Never skip. Never implement multiple major phases automatically.

| Phase | Name | One-line gate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Project Audit | `docs/project-audit.md` written; no architecture changes |
| 1 | Repository Foundation | `/frontend` `/backend` `/docs` `/infrastructure` `/scripts` run; health works |
| 2 | Database Foundation | Flyway: users, instruments, exchanges, sectors, industries |
| 3 | Instrument Master | Search, pagination, no duplicate instruments |
| 4 | Market Data Abstraction | `MarketDataProvider` mock; Quote/Candle/Timeframe |
| 5 | TimescaleDB | OHLCV hypertable + efficient range queries |
| 6 | Chart API | `GET /api/instruments/{id}/candles` validated |
| 7 | Frontend Chart | `StockChart.vue` from backend data only; no indicators |
| 8 | Technical Indicators | SMA EMA RSI MACD VWAP Bollinger; backend + tests |
| 9 | Fundamental Data | Normalized statements + derived metrics via backend |
| 10 | Fundamental Analytics | CAGRs, margins, trends; no misleading silent values |
| 11 | Valuation Engine | PE/PB/EV/EBITDA/PEG/DCF; assumptions visible |
| 12 | Algo Engine | Configurable `StockAlgorithm`; no hard-coded picks |
| 13 | Stock Score | Component scores + configurable weights 0–100 |
| 14 | Stock Page | Header, price, chart, score, fundamentals, valuation, risk |
| 15 | Watchlist | Multiple lists; add/remove/reorder; list score |
| 16 | Alerts | Price/score/valuation/technical/fundamental; notification port |
| 17 | Coverage Request | User requests + admin demand queue |
| 18 | User Algorithms | Controlled JSON/DSL rules; no user code execution |
| 19 | Screener | Filters + saved screens |
| 20 | AI Explanation | Structured inputs only; AI does not calculate |
| 21 | Portfolio without broker | CSV/Excel/manual; score, concentration, P&L |
| 22 | Kite Integration | Login, holdings, positions, orders, trades; tokens server-side |
| 23 | Broker Portfolio Sync | Scheduled/cached sync; no API hammering |
| 24 | Trading | Confirm screen; never auto-trade from algo signals |
| 25 | Backtesting | Bias controls; label simulated results |
| 26 | Production Hardening | Security, performance, reliability |
| 27 | Market Data Provider Selection | `docs/market-data-provider-decision.md`; no production adapter |
| 28 | Market Data Provider Integration | Licensed adapter behind `MarketDataProvider` only |
| 29 | Historical Data Import | Controlled job; small universe first |
| 30 | Historical Data Validation | `DataQualityService`; no silent bad data |
| 31 | Corporate Actions & Adjustments | Raw + adjusted; never destroy raw |
| 32 | Real-Time Market Data Pipeline | Vendor WS → our Redis/Timescale → our WS |
| 33 | Real-Time Frontend Streaming | Chart updates; LIVE only if fresh |
| 34 | Algo Research Dataset | Not against production HTTP |
| 35 | Backtesting Engine | No look-ahead; costs + slippage |
| 36 | Walk-Forward Validation | Label backtest vs out-of-sample |
| 37 | Production Algo Engine | Deterministic signals; AI explains only |
| 38 | Kite Developer/Broker Setup | `docs/kite-integration.md` before code |
| 39 | Kite Authentication | Tokens server-side, encrypted |
| 40 | Kite Portfolio Integration | Read-only first; map to `instrumentId` |
| 41 | Real-Time Portfolio | Our quotes + broker holdings |
| 42 | Kite Order Integration | Confirm screen; no silent algo orders |
| 43 | Paper Trading | Mandatory before live algo execution |
| 44 | Algo + User-Confirmed Trading | User presses BUY; no auto-trade |
| 45 | Monitoring & Observability | Data freshness + vendor health |
| 46 | Security & Production Hardening | Tokens, OWASP, backups |
| 47 | Billing / Subscription | `BillingProvider` — do not hard-code Razorpay |
| 48 | Production Launch | Limited 100–300 name universe |

## Phase 1 layout (only when authorized)

Backend packages: `controller` `service` `repository` `domain` `dto` `mapper` `config` `exception` `integration`

Frontend: `components` `views` `stores` `services` `router` `types` `composables` `layouts`

Also: `.env.example`, `.gitignore`, Docker, README, local dev instructions.

## Acceptance reminders

- Phase 4: do not connect a production market-data provider unless licensing is documented in `docs/data-licensing.md`.
- Phase 7: do not implement indicators.
- Phase 20: do not integrate OpenAI earlier.
- Phase 22: only after portfolio analytics works.
- Phase 24: only after broker sync is stable.

After finishing a phase, report `PHASE N COMPLETE` and the next recommended phase, then wait.

Phase 27–48: licensing and vendor adapters. Never implement a production market-data vendor until `docs/data-licensing.md` names a signed contract. Never use Kite as the market-data source.
